  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Friday)\nIssued at 130 PM MST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nAnother day of thick fog and low clouds around parts of western\nSD. These low visibilities and low cloud conditions have been \nslowly improving today for southwest SD but latest satellite\nimagery still shows northwest and central SD are stuck under \nclouds. And the occasional webcam shows the dense fog still \nlingering around in parts of far northwest South Dakota.\n\nLooking ahead to tonight, clouds will build back in for those who\nwere able to get some sun. Fog is a strong possibility for areas\naround the Black Hills and in northwest South Dakota. Wind speeds\nwill decrease and temps will dip into the 30s to low 40s.\n\nThe weekend will, more-or-less, be a continuation of the weather\nwe've been having. The early morning fog should fade out by\nmidday for most, winds will be breezy at times, and afternoon \ntemps will be above normal, reaching the 50s to low 60s.\n\nNext week will start off with similar weather but a weather\npattern change mid week will bring back the precip chances\nWednesday through Friday. Rain and rain/snow mix is likely at the\nstart of the pattern change but as colder air slides in from the \nnorth, rain/snow mix and snow is more likely.",
